    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FK94NRG8x7zRDHP6w2r8ca)_\n\nReplaces the plain rendering of heading tags in Org buffers with SVG chips from [svg-tag-mode](https://github.com/rougier/svg-tag-mode), driven by the existing tag groups.\n\n- **Install**: `use-package` with Elpaca, `svg-lib` from MELPA and `svg-tag-mode` from `rougier/svg-tag-mode`.\n- **Colour**: each chip uses `sp-org-tag-groups--chip-face`, so it takes the group colour from the theme-derived palette (#249); `unsorted` tags are neutral (#248). A theme change redraws the chips.\n- **Emoji**: the tag's emoji is shown in front of the chip in `sp-org-tag-groups-select-emoji-face` (#247), the same as `sp-select-note`. `sp-org-svg-tags-show-emoji` turns it off.\n- **How**: `svg-tag-mode` puts one display on one match, so there are three keywords: the tag name (chip), the colon before it (emoji) and the final colon (hidden). Matches outside the tags of a heading are ignored.\n- **Toggle / fallback**: `M-x sp-org-svg-tags-global-mode`, default from `sp-org-svg-tags-enable`. In a terminal frame, or without SVG support, it stays off and the tags are plain text.\n- **Interactions**: stays off if `org-modern-tag` is on (it is nil in `sp-org-appearance`); `org-indent` only sets a line prefix and `org-tags-column` is 0, so no alignment is needed.\n- Edited the doc (`sp-org-tag-groups.org`) and re-tangled `sp-org-tag-groups.el`. That also brings in `sp-org-tag-groups--explicit-groups`, which the committed `.el` lacked (same fix as #252, so the two will merge cleanly).\n\nTests: 4 new ERT tests, 9/9 pass in Emacs 29.3 batch (`-L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/ui`); I also ran the real `svg-tag-mode` font-lock over a sample buffer with a stub for the image. **Not run in a graphic frame**, so how the chips look and whether the emoji sit well with the chip height has to be checked on the Mac.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9xYXWjL6cySxZHmKU)_",
